# No-hardcoding policy. Machine-generated from the demo application's code
# index and committed so it is reviewed in the pull request; the check fails
# the build when the committed policy is stale. Regenerate it only with
# `pnpm check:no-hardcoding --update`; never hand-edit it.
/scripts/no-hardcoding.policy.json          @ConnerArdman
# The only human-curated input to that policy. Allowlisting a demo-specific
# identifier here would let the product encode demo knowledge and defeat the
# generalization acceptance test, so every addition needs deliberate review.
/scripts/no-hardcoding.allowlist.json       @ConnerArdman
# The only exemption channel for the secrets scanner. Adding a literal here is
# a security decision; a real credential must never be added.
/scripts/check-secrets.allowlist.json       @ConnerArdman

